terms.medium_def:
A woman from the tribe of Asher living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.17; 
referred to as Serah or Serah (KJV= Sarah) (שֶׂ֫רַח, שָׂ֫רַח); 
daughter of Asher; 
a sister of Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi and Beriah.

A woman living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.11.29; 
only referred to as Milcah (מִלְכָּה); 
daughter of Haran; 
a sister of Lot and Iscah; 
wife of Nahor; 
mother of Uz, Buz, Kemuel, Chesed, Hazo, Pildash, Jidlaph and Bethuel.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.14.49; 
only referred to as Malchi-shua (מַלְכִּישׁוּעַ); 
son of Saul and Ahinoam; 
a brother of Jonathan, Abinadab, Merab and Michal; 
half-brother of: Ish-bosheth, Armoni and Mephibosheth. § a son of king Saul of Israel

A woman from the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.26.33; 
only referred to as Milcah (מִלְכָּה); 
daughter of Zelophehad; 
a sister of Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah and Tirzah.

A man from the tribe of Asher living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.17; 
referred to as Malchiel (מַלְכִּיאֵל), or Malchielite (מַלְכִּיאֵלִי); 
son of Beriah; 
a brother of Heber; 
father or founder of Birzaith. § the son of Beriah and grandson of Asher

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.21.1; 
referred to as Malchiah or Malchiah (KJV= Melchiah, NIV= Malkijah) (מַלְכִּיָּהוּ); 
father of Pashhur.

A male deity in the Old Testament; 
called Molech (מֹ֫לֶךְ); or Milcom (KJV= "their king;" NIV= Molek) or Milcom (KJV= Malcham; NIV= Molek) (מֶ֫לֶךְ); or Milcom (NIV= Molek) (מִלכֹּם); or Moloch (NIV= Molek) (Μολόχ) § the god of the Ammonites and Phoenicians to whom some Israelites sacrificed their infants in the valley of Hinnom
1a) also 'Molech'

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.36.26; 
only referred to as Hammelech (הַמֶּלֶךְ); 
father of Jerahmeel and Malchijah. § A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.36.26; 
father of: Jerahmeel (H3396I) and Malchijah (H4441H); also translated "the king";

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.35; 
only referred to as Melech (מֶ֫לֶךְ); 
son of Micah; 
a brother of Pithon, Tarea and Ahaz. § a Benjamite, the 2nd son of Micah and grandson of Mephibosheth

A priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.12; 
only referred to as Malchijah (מַלְכִּיָּהוּ); 
a brother of Jerahmeel; 
a son of Hammelech; 
father of Pashhur.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.44; 
only referred to as Malluch (מַלּוּךְ); 
a son of Hashabiah; 
father of Abdi. § a priest who returned from exile with Zerubbabel

A man from the tribe of Asher living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.17; 
referred to as Malchiel (מַלְכִּיאֵל), or Malchielite (מַלְכִּיאֵלִי); 
son of Beriah; 
a brother of Heber; 
father or founder of Birzaith. § an Asherite and a descendant of Malchiel, the grandson of Asher

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.40; 
only referred to as Malchijah (מַלְכִּיָּהוּ); 
a son of Jeatherai; 
father of Baaseiah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.11; 
only referred to as Malchijah (מַלְכִּיָּהוּ); 
a son of Harim.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.14; 
only referred to as Malchijah (מַלְכִּיָּהוּ); 
a son of Rechab.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.18; 
only referred to as Malchiram (מַלְכִּירָם); 
son of Shealtiel(?); 
a brother of Pedaiah, Shenazzar, Jekamiah, Hoshama and Nedabiah. § son of king Jehoiachin of Judah

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.9; 
only referred to as Malcam (מַלְכָּם); 
son of Shaharaim and Hodesh; 
a brother of Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Jeuz, Sachia, Mirmah, Abitub and Elpaal. § a Benjamite, son of Shaharaim by his wife Hodesh

A woman from the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.18; 
only referred to as Hammolecheth (הַמֹּלֶכֶת); 
daughter of Machir; 
a sister of Gilead, daughter_of_Machir, Peresh and Sheresh; 
mother of Ishhod, Abiezer and Mahlah. § daughter of Machir and sister of Gilead

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.11.42; 
only referred to as Shiza (שִׁיזָא); 
father of Adina. § a Reubenite, father of Adina, one of David's mighty warriors

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, only mentioned at Gen.49.10; 
only referred to as Shiloh (שִׁילֹה). §A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, only mentioned at Gen.49.10; also translated "tribute" 
meaning uncertain

A man from the tribe of Judah(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.20; 
only referred to as Shimon (שִׁימוֹן); 
father of Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-hanan, Tilon. § a Judaite, father of Amnon, Rinnah, Ben-Hanan, and Tilon

A male deity in the Old Testament; 
called Baal (בַּעַל); or Baal of Peor (KJV= Baal , Baal-peor; NIV= Baal of Peor) or Baal-peor or Peor (ESV, NIV= Baal of Peor) (בַּ֫עַל פְּעוֹר); or Baal (Βάαλ) § esp. lord, specif. as divine name, Baal
supreme male divinity of the Phoenicians or Canaanites

An Edomite king living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.38; 
only referred to as Baal-hanan (בַּ֫עַל חָנָן); 
a son of Achbor.

David's compatriots living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.4.2; 
only referred to as Baanah (בַּעֲנָה); 
son of Rimmon; 
a brother of Rechab.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.30; 
only referred to as Baal (בַּ֫עַל); 
son of Abiel and Maacah; 
a brother of Kish, Ner, Abdon, Zur, Nadab, Gedor, Ahio, Zecher and Mikloth. § Baal = "lord"

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.23.29; 
only referred to as Baanah (בַּעֲנָה); 
father of Heleb.

Emperor living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Dan.5.1; 
referred to as Belshazzar (בֵּֽלְאשַׁצַּר, בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר), or Belshazzar (Aramiac בֵּֽלְאשַׁצַּר, בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר); 
a son of Nebuchadnezzar. § king of Babylon at the time of its fall; he to whom Daniel interpreted the writing on the wall

A man from the tribe of Reuben living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.5.5; 
only referred to as Baal (בַּ֫עַל); 
a son of Reaiah; 
father of Beerah. § Baal = "lord"

David's son from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.5.16; 
referred to as Eliada (אֶלְיָדָע), or Beeliada (בְּעֶלְיָדָע); 
son of David; 
a brother of Amnon, Chileab, Absalom, Adonijah, Shephatiah, Ithream, Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon, Ibhar, Elishua, Nepheg, Japhia, Elishama, Eliphelet, Tamar, Elpelet, Nogah and Jerimoth. § a son of David, born in Jerusalem, elsewhere named 'Eliada'

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ki.4.12; 
only referred to as Baana (בַּעֲנָא); 
son of Ahilud; 
a brother of Jehoshaphat.

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ki.4.16; 
only referred to as Baana (בַּעֲנָא); 
a son of Hushai.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.4; 
only referred to as Baana (בַּעֲנָא); 
father of Zadok.

David's brother from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.2.14; 
only referred to as Raddai (רַדַּי); 
son of Jesse; 
a brother of David, Eliab, Abinadab, Shimeah, Nethanel, Ozem, Zeruiah, Abigail(?) and Elihu. § the 5th son of Jesse and brother of David
